      "worked": "Take $f(x)=x^2$ with domain $\\mathbb R$ and $g(x)=\\sqrt{x}$ with domain $[0,\\infty)$.\n\nFor $x\\ge0$,\n$$\\begin{align*}f(g(x))&=(\\sqrt{x})^2\\\\f(g(x))&=x.\\end{align*}$$\nFor $x\\in\\mathbb R$,\n$$\\begin{align*}g(f(x))&=\\sqrt{x^2}\\\\g(f(x))&=|x|.\\end{align*}$$\nAt $x=-1$, $g(f(-1))=1\\ne-1$, so the reverse composition is not the identity on the domain of $f$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
